{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SymbolRenderingMode"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Type Property","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI19SymbolRenderingModeV12hierarchicalACvpZ","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"hierarchical","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SymbolRenderingMode","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI19SymbolRenderingModeV"}],"title":"hierarchical","symbolKind":"property"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"hierarchical","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SymbolRenderingMode","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI19SymbolRenderingModeV","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SymbolRenderingMode"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenSwiftUI fills the first layer with the foreground style, and the others"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the secondary, and tertiary variants of the foreground style. You can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specify these styles explicitly using the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View\/foregroundStyle(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View\/foregroundStyle(_:_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifiers. If you only specify"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a primary foreground style, OpenSwiftUI automatically derives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the others from that style. For example, you can render a filled"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exclamation mark triangle with purple as the tint color for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exclamation mark, and lower opacity purple for the triangle:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["Image(systemName: \"exclamationmark.triangle.fill\")","    .symbolRenderingMode(.hierarchical)","    .foregroundStyle(Color.purple)"]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/symbolrenderingmode\/hierarchical"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A mode that renders symbols as multiple layers, with different opacities"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applied to the foreground style."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SymbolRenderingMode\/hierarchical"},"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"OpenSwiftUI","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/SymbolRenderingMode/hierarchical":{"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"hierarchical","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SymbolRenderingMode","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI19SymbolRenderingModeV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SymbolRenderingMode\/hierarchical","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A mode that renders symbols as multiple layers, with different opacities","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applied to the foreground style.","type":"text"}],"title":"hierarchical","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/symbolrenderingmode\/hierarchical","type":"topic"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/SymbolRenderingMode":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SymbolRenderingMode","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/SymbolRenderingMode","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A symbol rendering mode.","type":"text"}],"title":"SymbolRenderingMode","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/symbolrenderingmode","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SymbolRenderingMode","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"}}}